Quest 3: The Scaffolding

You are stepping out of Python/Localhost scripts and into a compiled, strongly-typed systems language. Respect the directory structure.

Your Orders:

Open your terminal in the Sanctum directory.

Run go mod init github.com/{your_github_username}/sanctum (Replace with your actual username).

Create the directory tree: mkdir -p cmd/server

Create the entry point: touch cmd/server/main.go

Write the server using only the standard library (net/http).

Listen on port 8080.

Create a single route: GET /health that returns {"status": "Sanctum is alive"} with an HTTP 200 OK.

No frameworks. If I see import "github.com/gin-gonic/gin", I will reject the PR. You need to feel how HTTP works at the raw socket and multiplexer level before you earn the right to use abstractions.

Write the code. Run go run cmd/server/main.go. Test it with curl http://localhost:8080/health.

Show me the contents of main.go when it is breathing.
